  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct Aid Program - Kiribati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Direct Aid Program (DAP) is a flexible small grants program, up to $20,000 per grant, administered by the Australian High Commission in Kiribati. The DAP supports community-based projects implemented by grantees such as community groups, local church groups and non-government organisations. DAP projects include community and/or rural development, education, gender equality, disabilities, youth, human rights, the environment, small-scale infrastructure, economic empowerment, ad hoc humanitarian relief and many others.</narrative>
  </description>
